.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kldload-db: no VM named NAME; nothing changed"
.It "kldload-db: no node named HOST; nothing changed"
.It "kldload-db: no deployment N; nothing changed"
Nothing matched; check the name.
.It "kldload-db: no live VM named NAME"
From
.Cm vm-show :
never registered, or deleted.
.It "kldload-db: attempt to write a readonly database"
Run as a user outside the
.Ql kldload
group, or before a root run has set the group up.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kld 1 ,
.Xr sqlite3 1 ,
.Xr kldload-estate 8 ,
.Xr kldload-inventory 8 ,
.Xr kldload-networks 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-delete 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-26 the schema lived in the web console and was created only
when it started; on a host where it never had, every write here failed
with
.Dq no such table ,
every caller ignored it, and the estate was empty.
On 2026-09-28 a control plane rebuilt under its old name kept its dead
predecessor's mesh key and read as off the mesh; registering a deleted
name clears it since.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: a status update that matched no row
returned success.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The database records what it is told: nothing here checks that a machine
exists.
.Xr kldload-networks 8
reconciles it with libvirt.
.Pp
.Ql bob_conversations
holds the web console's assistant conversations;
.Cm dump
does not print it.
